<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lucius Cornelius Balbus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 19 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lucius Cornelius Balbus was a Roman general and proconsul of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. In 19 BCE he led a punitive expedition against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garamantian-empire">Garamantian Empire</a>, capturing fifteen Garamantian settlements including the capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garama">Garama</a>. He received a triumph in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, the last ever awarded to a general outside the imperial family.</p></div>
